CLASS net/minecraft/unmapped/C_ncfucati net/minecraft/test/TestContext
	COMMENT Context for a test instance.<br>
	COMMENT Contains methods for converting between relative test space and absolute world
	COMMENT space, along with methods for defining when a test passes or fails.<br>
	COMMENT Methods annotated with {@code @GameTest} receive the context for the test
	COMMENT instance they're testing.
	COMMENT <p>
	COMMENT The location and rotation of test instances vary between runs, so tests use
	COMMENT locations relative the test structure's bottom north west corner for
	COMMENT consistency.<br>
	COMMENT {@code TestContext} methods take positions/boxes/etc. in this relative space.<br>
	COMMENT However if you need to call methods of non-test classes that take those as input,
	COMMENT use {@link #getAbsolute} methods to convert to absolute
	COMMENT world space.<br>
	COMMENT Conversely, if non-test class's methods return those types, use
	COMMENT {@link #getRelative} methods to convert to relative test space.
	COMMENT <p>
	COMMENT A tests' success is controlled by
	COMMENT {@link net.minecraft.test.GameTestException GameTestException}s.<br>
	COMMENT The {@code check...} and {@code expect...} methods are reusable ways to express
	COMMENT common expectations, while the {@code assert...} and
	COMMENT {@code create/throwException...} methods provide ways to define custom
	COMMENT expectations.<br>
	COMMENT Use {@link #createTaskSequence()} to define expectations accross time.
	COMMENT
	COMMENT @see net.minecraft.test.TestTaskSequence TestTaskSequence
